          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: A witness observed on August 7, 2012, at approximately 9:31 PM, an O-E movement in the sky of a bright, high-intensity spherical object. The account of the observation strongly suggests the passage of a large low-orbit satellite (300 to 400 km). However, a check against the global satellite database shows no correlation with this observation. It could be an unlisted object (military satellite). Due to the lack of precise information, the GEIPAN classifies this unusual case as \"C\".",
